  "notes": "Strict 1:1 with the portal DIC tool (modules/tools_tab/tools/dic_tool.R). All constants come from the constants table; the request carries no override for h_co2_29815k / gas_const_r_mol / vial_volume / h3po4_added, because the portal has none (constants_come_from_the_table_only pins that a perturbed table value moves the result, and that the caller cannot override it). lab_temp_mode is the portal's 'Use lab temp constant' checkbox (dic_tool.R:187-191): 'cst' reads lab_temp_avg_degC and ignores the entered cell, 'db' reads the cell and yields nothing when it is blank; the functions' unreachable 'default' fallback mode is not offered. Each replicate cell is its own param, named '{portal column}_rep_{A|B}' after the portal's own lab_dic_*_A / lab_dic_*_B columns, so the letter travels in the field name and a blank cell cannot move a value onto another replicate (lone_replicate_b_stays_on_b sends the cells of single_replicate_emits_A_and_average on B and gets the same numbers under DIC_B / d13C_DIC_B). Replicates A and B are looped unconditionally (dic_tool.R:194-227), so a single entry still emits DIC_A / d13C_DIC_A alongside the average. No input is required: a blank cell reaches calcDIC/calcd13DIC, which return NA (calculation_functions.R:367, :449), and the portal simply shows an empty row (blank_weights_are_accepted_and_yield_nothing, replicate_b_blank_weights_are_treated_like_a). calcMean/calcSd use na.rm, so with one d13co2 value the average is that value and the sd is 'KEEP OLD' (one_sided_d13c); the portal would carry the stored value forward for 'KEEP OLD', but this tool is stateless, so the key is omitted instead. Every case lists every key it does not expect, so a regression that starts emitting an extra replicate or std is caught. NaN and Inf are values the portal writes to the table (calcDIC:357-362 guards only is.na and divisor != 0), so the wrapper emits them: overflowing_co2_gives_an_infinite_dic produces DIC_A = Inf and DIC_avg = Inf, unbounded_headspace_gives_a_nan_replicate produces DIC_A = NaN and d13C_DIC_A = NaN. Both serialise to JSON null and the API drops nulls, so they are listed as absent even though the portal would display them; the NaN case also pins that calcMean's na.rm drops a NaN replicate, leaving the average equal to replicate B. An unrecognised lab_temp_mode is normalised to the 'db' default in the wrapper, so the functions' 'default' branch cannot run; no case exercises it because the enum gate rejects any other value before the script is reached. Golden values cross-checked against an independent implementation of calcDIC:335-364 / calcd13DIC:430-444 as well as the live runner."
